## SQ-CMG-01 | Magic's and Equipment's mixins apply from their own jsons, none from creativeengineering.mixins.json
@group A
@commands Boot 2: `grep -E "creativemagic.mixins.json\|creativeequipment.mixins.json\|creativeengineering.mixins.json" logs/latest.log`; `grep -c "from creativemagic.mixins.json" logs/debug.log`; same for `creativeequipment`; mod list
@pass No mixin apply error; Magic's 7 and Equipment's 20 mixins apply (gated ones only with their mod); none of them from `creativeengineering.mixins.json`
@fails a mixin left in or missing from a json; package rename missed
@jars creativebrewing creativecommon creativedelight creativedevtools creativeengineering creativemagic
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
bootreject (creativemagic|creativeequipment)\.mixins\.json.*(rror|ailed|could not)
shell grep -cE "from (mixins\.)?creativemagic\.mixins\.json" logs/debug.log; grep -cE "from (mixins\.)?creativeequipment\.mixins\.json" logs/debug.log; grep -E "creativeengineering\.mixins\.json" logs/debug.log | grep -oE "Mixing \S+" | sort -u | head -30
look Magic: up to 13 common mixins in its json, Equipment up to 23 (gated ones only with their mod; a mixin with several targets counts more than once); the creativeengineering list holds only Engineering's own mixins (17 common), none of Magic's or Equipment's class names

## SQ-CMG-02 | [botania] carried into Magic's new file, the nine Equipment tables into Equipment's, values kept
@group A
@commands Same boot: read `config/creativemagic-common.toml`, `config/creativeequipment-common.toml`, `config/creativeengineering-common.toml`; restart, read again
@pass `[swaps] config sections [botania] carried over` and the nine Equipment tables carried; `trinketCaseAnyItem = false` and the edited `wearThreshold` in the new files; after the restart the CE file has none of the ten tables, `[damage_tags]` still there
@fails `ConfigRename.carrySections` not reached before Forge loads configs; a table name in `SECTIONS` misspelt
@jars creativebrewing creativecommon creativedelight creativedevtools creativeengineering creativemagic
@from batches/r1113/c2_l1.qb
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections \[botania\] carried over from creativeengineering-common.toml to creativemagic-common.toml
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections \[dragon_gear, air_brake, stepstool, crafting, armor_enchantability, shields, bonemeal_charm, bottled_air, backpackSkins\] carried over from creativeengineering-common.toml to creativeequipment-common.toml
bootreject could not (carry|merge) config sections
shell grep -nE "trinketCaseAnyItem" config/creativemagic-common.toml; grep -nE "wearThreshold *=" config/creativeequipment-common.toml; grep -nE "^\[" config/creativeequipment-common.toml | tr '\n' ' '
look trinketCaseAnyItem = false and wearThreshold = 4.5 in the new files (Forge's correction keeps them); Equipment's file also has its later tables ([tooltips], [copper_poisoning], [armor_overflow]) added at their defaults

## SQ-CMG-03 | Magic and Equipment startup packs load after the pack folder; no global missing, no NCH.cfg section miss
@group A
@commands Same boot: `grep -E "startup script packs in order\|creativemagic\|creativeequipment\|NCH.cfg" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log \| head -30`
@pass Packs `creativemagic` and `creativeequipment` load after the pack folder; no `global.CMG missing` / `global.CEQ missing`; no `no ... section in any registered config` (end_gear.js reads `CRAFTING.FELSIC_*`); no script error
@fails `cmg_core.js` / `ceq_core.js` not in the jar; `registerConfig` class name wrong
@jars creativebrewing creativecommon creativedelight creativedevtools creativeengineering creativemagic
@from batches/r1113/c2_a1.qb
shell grep -nE "startup script packs in order|creativemagic|creativeequipment|NCH.cfg|global\.(CMG|CEQ) missing|in any registered config" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | head -30 | cut -c1-260
kjsreject global\.(CMG|CEQ) missing|section in any registered config
look packs line lists creativemagic and creativeequipment after the pack folder; no script error lines for either

## SQ-CMG-04
@group A
@commands Same save: `/data get block` the portal frame; light a new obsidian frame with `minecraft:flint_and_steel` and with `creativeengineering:flint_and_terrasteel` (`/give`); `/recipe` or the recipe dump for `creativemagic:` ids
@pass Ordinary flame fails and the frame turns to crying obsidian; Dark Fire opens the portal; existing portal blocks still there; Flint and Terrasteel, Ender Storage, CEI machine and sculk recipes exist under `creativemagic:`
@fails `PortalFailureHandler` subscriber not registered (modid); `DARK_FIRE` not registered
@jars creativebrewing creativecommon creativedelight creativedevtools creativeengineering creativemagic
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> forceload add 352 288 384 304
# two obsidian frames (inside 2 x 3), one per igniter
> fill 360 -61 300 363 -56 300 minecraft:obsidian
> fill 361 -60 300 362 -57 300 minecraft:air
> fill 370 -61 300 373 -56 300 minecraft:obsidian
> fill 371 -60 300 372 -57 300 minecraft:air
> cdevtest use 361 -61 300 held=minecraft:flint_and_steel face=up
sleep 1
> cdevtest state 361 -60 300
> cdevtest count 360 -61 300 363 -56 300 minecraft:crying_obsidian
> cdevtest use 371 -61 300 held=creativemagic:flint_and_terrasteel face=up
sleep 1
> cdevtest state 371 -60 300
> cdevtest recipes creativemagic: max=400
expect verb=count block=minecraft:crying_obsidian n=[1-9]
reject verb=state pos=361,-60,300 state="?minecraft:nether_portal
expect verb=state pos=371,-60,300 state="?minecraft:nether_portal
expect verb=recipes id=creativemagic:\S*flint_and_terrasteel
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0
look recipes list has Ender Storage, CEI machine and sculk recipes under creativemagic:; portal blocks of the old save (same save as SQ-CMG-01) still standing is checked by the runner where that save's portal was
